codex
I found a concrete trust-boundary risk that the existing differential suite does not exercise: `scopedDirs` caches an ancestor handle. If that directory is renamed and replaced after the handle is cached, subsequent files are read from the detached old directory, while the legacy root-relative open resolves the replacement and detects the identity change. I’m adding a focused regression that accepts either re-resolution or a fail-closed error, but rejects reading the detached tree; this is directly tied to the task’s mutation/race acceptance criterion.
